Run the Higurashi delivery workflow for these exact arguments:

`$ARGUMENTS`

Accept only `<WORK-ITEM-ID>`, `<WORK-ITEM-ID> --plan-only`, or
`<WORK-ITEM-ID> --repair`. Treat the work-item ID as opaque input, never as a
path or shell fragment. Reject missing, reordered, or additional arguments.

Load the `higurashi-deliver` skill and follow it as the authoritative workflow
contract. The Pi adapter uses the current Pi session as its coordinator and
does not require a subagent extension. If a trusted Pi subagent extension is
installed, it may be used for the named Higurashi roles, but it must preserve
the same one-task, read-only reviewer, bounded-loop, and anti-bypass contracts.

When the user explicitly authorizes a commit, follow the skill's completed-
candidate rule: commit only after inspection reports `kind: complete`, including
an explicitly deferred completion with its `Completion-Note` and follow-up
requirements. Never commit a blocked or repair-state artifact, and never push,
publish, or release without separate authorization.
